.TH TV 1 "2026-10-27" "tv 1.28.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tv \- display images in a text terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tv
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tv
displays JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP, BMP and netpbm (PBM, PGM, PPM) images in a
text terminal, including terminals without graphics such as serial
consoles. Images are drawn with half block characters (two pixels per
character cell) or with ASCII characters, and resized to fit the terminal.
Animated GIF and WebP images are played in place.
.PP
The format is detected from the content of the file, not from its
extension. With \fIFILE\fR \fB\-\fR, the image is read from the standard
input. Pipes and devices can be read too.
.PP
JPEG photos are rotated following their EXIF orientation. Transparent
pixels are drawn over a black background.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Size
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-size\fR=\fICOLS\fBx\fIROWS\fR
Terminal size, when it can't be detected (see \fBTERMINAL SIZE\fR).
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR=\fICOLS\fR
Maximum width of the image in columns.
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-height\fR=\fIROWS\fR
Maximum height of the image in rows.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-upscale\fR
Enlarge small images up to the maximum size. Images are only shrunk by
default.
.TP
\fB\-\-fit\fR=\fIMODE\fR
Terminal dimensions limiting the size of the image: \fBboth\fR (default),
\fBwidth\fR, \fBheight\fR or \fBnone\fR.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-center\fR
Center the image horizontally.
.SS Colors
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-colors\fR=\fIMODE\fR
\fBtruecolor\fR, \fB256\fR, \fB16\fR, \fB8\fR or \fBmono\fR. In mono no
escape sequence is written at all, only blocks. \fBauto\fR (default)
chooses from the environment (see \fBENVIRONMENT\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dither\fR=\fIMODE\fR
How colors are approximated with few colors: \fBauto\fR (default:
\fBfs\fR for still images, \fBordered\fR for animations), \fBfs\fR
(Floyd-Steinberg), \fBordered\fR (stable between frames) or \fBnone\fR
(smallest output).
.SS Characters
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-ascii\fR
Draw with ASCII characters: one character per pixel, chosen by brightness
in " .:\-=+*#%@" and colored with the pixel color, except in mono. Used
automatically when the locale is not UTF-8.
.TP
\fB\-\-utf8\fR
Draw with half blocks even if the locale is not UTF-8.
.SS Animation
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-loop\fR
Play animations until Ctrl-C. They are played once by default.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-plays\fR=\fIN\fR
Play animations \fIN\fR times.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-file\-loop\fR
Play animations as many times as the file says: GIF NETSCAPE2.0 loop
count (repeated after the first play, like browsers) or WebP loop count.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fps\fR=\fIN\fR
Draw at most \fIN\fR frames per second. Frames are skipped but the
animation keeps its speed, useful on slow links.
.TP
\fB\-\-frame\fR=\fIN\fR
Only display the frame \fIN\fR (from 1) of an animation.
.SS Other
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Don't print the information line under images.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-title\fR
Print the file name before each image (\fB==> \fIfile\fB <==\fR).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-info\fR
Only print the format, size (after EXIF rotation), channels, frames, loop
count and EXIF orientation of each image, one line per file.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show the help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version and the formats built in, and exit.
.SH TERMINAL SIZE
The terminal size is searched in this order: the \fB\-s\fR option, the
kernel (\fBTIOCGWINSZ\fR), the \fBCOLUMNS\fR and \fBLINES\fR environment
variables, then the terminal itself: the cursor is moved to the bottom
right corner and its position is asked. Serial consoles often report a
0x0 size to the kernel, but most terminal emulators (picocom, minicom,
screen...) answer this request. When the window size in pixels is known,
the image height is corrected for the font proportions.
.PP
When the size is unknown (output redirected to a file), images keep their
size unless \fB\-w\fR or \fB\-H\fR is given.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, the default color mode is \fBmono\fR.
.TP
.B TERM
\fBdumb\fR gives \fBmono\fR, a value containing \fB256color\fR gives
\fB256\fR colors, any other terminal \fB16\fR colors.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
\fBtruecolor\fR or \fB24bit\fR gives \fBtruecolor\fR.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LANG
When the locale is not UTF-8, images are drawn with ASCII characters.
.TP
.BR COLUMNS ", " LINES
Terminal size when the kernel doesn't know it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every file was displayed.
.TP
.B 1
At least one file could not be displayed, or invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 130
Stopped with Ctrl-C.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tv photo.jpg
Display a photo, resized to fit the terminal.
.TP
.B tv \-c 16 \-f 5 \-l animation.gif
Play an animation forever over a slow serial link.
.TP
.B ssh board cat /tmp/capture.png | tv \-
Display an image of a remote board.
.TP
.B tv \-i *.jpg
Print the size and orientation of photos without drawing them.
.TP
.B tv \-a \-c mono \-w 60 logo.png > logo.txt
Write an ASCII art version of an image, without any escape sequence.
.SH NOTES
Errors are written on the standard error as \fBtv: \fIfile\fB: \fImessage\fR.
.PP
The JPEG, PNG, GIF and WebP decoders can be disabled at build time
(\fBmake WITH_JPEG=0\fR...), BMP and netpbm are always built. \fBtv \-V\fR
lists the formats built in.
